BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Beach Metro Community News
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260912T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260912T143000
DTSTAMP:20260828T133738Z
CREATED:20260827T220433Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260828T133738Z
UID:52699-1789207200-1789223400@beachmetro.com
SUMMARY:Shades of Blue: A Collaborative Cyanotype Workshop
DESCRIPTION:☀️💙 Ever wanted to make art with sunlight? Join us for Shades of Blue: A Collaborative Cyanotype Workshop\, a hands-on workshop exploring the magic of solar printing! \n🌿🧵Learn how to create beautiful Prussian-blue cyanotype prints by arranging botanicals and other flat objects onto fabric and exposing them to sunlight. You’ll leave with a print of your own\, plus contribute a piece to a collaborative quilt that will be displayed at East End Arts! \nNo experience necessary — just curiosity and a willingness to try something new! All materials provided\, though you’re welcome to bring your own botanicals or flat objects to print with. \n🗓️ Saturday\, September 12\, 2026\n🕙 10 AM–2:30 PM\n📍 St. Matthew’s Clubhouse\, 450 Broadview Ave\n🎟️ Space is limited — pre-register to save your spot! \n🎟️ Register here: https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfsEiVrFn6mwdv2CAJMu-DlUGiD8G5YMeUUK2uFzLm1hInGYA/viewform \n✨ About the Artist\nSahar Alamgir is a multidisciplinary Pakistani artist based in Toronto who works with found and inherited fabrics to create quilts and other textile works. Her practice explores the stories and memories held within materials\, and she’s recently been experimenting with sun-printing and natural dyes.
URL:https://beachmetro.com/event/shades-of-blue-a-collaborative-cyanotype-workshop/
LOCATION:St. Matthew’s Clubhouse\, 450 Broadview Avenue\, Toronto\, M4K 2N3
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://d28bcn7yu97icd.cloudfront.net/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/27180436/ArtLabs-Poster_Final_Sahar-Alamgirsm.png
ORGANIZER;CN="East End Arts":MAILTO:info@eastendarts.ca
END:VEVENT
